#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Second dispatch point: the change was approved and merged, and the root of the site has been rebuilt from main. A failing main build can look like a green run from inside the repo. `note` rather than `claim`: the branch-watch bean already exists, and whether the publish SUCCEEDED is not this step's judgement (the build reports its own exit code). A bean is not closed on someone else's say-so, so the step records what it observed and leaves the verdict to the watcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The approval did not end in a merge. Nothing is deployed and branches/<slug>/ is left up; a later push to the branch starts a new run of this process."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The owner says \"merge it\", and only then is the branch merged. Merge to main triggers: 1. the main site rebuilds with the changes; 2. the staging preview's cleanup runs; 3. the review comments committed on the feature branch land on main, as the review record."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Was the PR merged? `Yes` removes the branches/<slug>/ preview; `No` ends this run at End_NotMerged without deploying and without looping back into review (the lane note says why); the preview stays in place, and the next push starts a new run."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When the PR is merged or closed, the cleanup job removes the branches/<slug>/ directory from gh-pages so stale previews don't accumulate."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/content-change-review-publish.bpmn:120
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""
